# The affiant-protocol ref this repository's conformance driver is pinned to.
#
# Versions of the rulebook (https://github.com/Sakwala/affiant-protocol) are git tags.
# The pin is the v0.1.3 tag, and `commit` records what that tag points at, so a reader
# can check one against the other with no network. While a version's text is on the
# rulebook's default branch and its tag has not been cut, `tag` is empty and the COMMIT
# is the pin: a commit is as immutable as a tag and, unlike a tag, cannot be moved
# under a running build.
#
# Changing this file is a reviewable diff in this repository's own history: a format
# change arrives as a pull request, never as a silent upstream shift under a build.
#
# `conformance/sync.sh` reads this file. `conformance/sync.sh --verify` re-checks the
# vendored copy under tests/Affiant.Conformance.Tests/protocol/ against SHA256SUMS,
# which is what CI runs, so a local edit to a vendored fixture cannot pass unnoticed.

repository=https://github.com/Sakwala/affiant-protocol
commit=cfb476431aa4d6bbaef9cacbce5bab75053e67c8
tag=v0.1.3
tag_note=v0.1.3 was cut on the commit above on 2026-09-08: PV-3 now says WHO establishes presence. "The value is literally present in the utterance" is a property of two strings, so the implementation establishes it from the unmodified turn - a hit is an occurrence of the value text under an ASCII-only case fold (A-Z against a-z; every other code point compares exactly) whose neighbouring code points are none of L*, M*, Nd, Pc - and grades Conversation, bound to an utterance-span whose offsets are UTF-16 code units of the utterance and whose hash is SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of the utterance's own substring at that span. A port's `presence` and `utteranceSpan` become optional in the fixture schema and are hints the implementation verifies the same way: a span is used only when it is itself a hit, an unconfirmed `literal` is Inferred, and a value the port said nothing about is Conversation when it is there to read. A value that is null, an object, an array, the empty string or a non-finite number is nothing reported for that field. Five gate fixtures are authored at this tag and one, sequence-a/picker-external-binding, is amended; the field matcher gains `utteranceSpan`; conformance/ORACLE.md gains a second table, the negative oracle against dotnet 1.0.0-beta.3.
vendored=tests/Affiant.Conformance.Tests/protocol
